\tag{fdip}
\title{Contexts and background stacks}
\date{2026-11-03}

\p{Which families of observables admit a joint classical value?}

\p{A context is a commutative unital *-subalgebra of a matrix
algebra. A global point assigns a character to every context in a
family, and the assigned characters agree on shared elements. The
following section shows that 6 contexts cut out by one square in
#{M_4(\mathbb C)} have no global point, while each context
separately does. Whether this obstruction organises the
[selectors](fdip-005K) remains open. The last section remains
speculative.}

